tial if I complete with middle tiles = 2 points\n\nReason: T1 is the most isolated tile in my hand. Discarding it maintains maximum flexibility with my remaining tiles, which can form multiple chow combinations (T2-T3-T4 potential, T6-T7-T8, T7-T8-T9). Keeping pairs of T3, T6, T8, T9 gives me multiple waiting patterns. The hand is moving toward a Full Flush (24 points) with all Bamboo tiles, which is a high-value pattern.\n\nAnswer: Play T1"}
